  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Office of Research and Development (ORD): Marshall Aid Commemoration Commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the efforts of the British government to conduct the EPA-Cooperative Marshall Scholars Programme, which provides opportunities for US students with excellent academic records to pursue up to 5 years of graduate level work leading to a PhD or equivalent degree in an environmental field with global or international significance, studying, for example, international collaborative approaches to solving challenges of clean air, clean water, and environmental stewardship. The first 2 years of this study are to be conducted at a university in the UK at the expense of the British government. EPA pays for the final 3 years of the scholarship, either in the UK or US.</narrative>
  </description>
